mode: "100644"
text: "# The reality of CapCut in 2026 (verify-quarterly)\n\nPlans, gated features, and terms shift fast here — attribute everything, **verify-quarterly**, and check in-app\nbefore building a workflow on any specific feature or price.\n\n## What it is (and its deliberate ceiling)\nCapCut (ByteDance — TikTok's parent) is the default short-form editor for a huge share of TikTok/Reels/Shorts\ncontent: timeline editing, beat-sync, auto-captions, background removal, text-to-speech, AI effects, weekly\ntrend/template updates, and phone → desktop → browser sync. Its practical ceiling is **~15 minutes by design** —\nit's optimized for short-form, not long-form (route podcasts/documentaries to Descript/Resolve/Premiere; reviews\nconsistently note the hybrid pipeline: master long-form elsewhere, cut social pieces in CapCut). Banned in India\nsince June 2020. (per 2026 reviews — BIGVU, max-productive, pixflow; verify-quarterly)\n\n## The 2026 feature stack (attribute; verify-quarterly)\nAuto-captions (fast; **accuracy pass required** on accents/technical vocab; free tier ~10 min captioned video per\nproject, Pro unlimited; SRT/VTT/ASS export) · AI background removal (real-time; fine hair still artifacts) · AI\nmotion/camera tracking · vocal isolation + flicker removal (Pro) · text-to-speech + AI avatars · Long-Video-to-\nShorts (clip suggestions) · script generator (generic voice — the brand voice comes from `voice-builder`) ·\nkeyframes/beat-sync · exports MP4 (H.264/H.265)/MOV, 24–60fps, 4K on Pro.\n\n## Plans + the paywall reality (sources conflict — reconcile honestly)\nEarly-2026 restructure split the old single Pro tier: **Standard ≈ $9.99/mo** and **Pro ≈ $19.99/mo (~$15/mo\nbilled annually)** with 4K, the full AI suite, ~1,200 AI points/mo, 1TB cloud; some sources still cite $7.99–9.99\nPro (regional/legacy variation) — **don't quote a price as fact; verify in-app.** Two documented frustrations\n(attribute — Trustpilot/BIGVU): **features migrate behind Pro over time** (the classic failure: build the edit,\nhit the paywall at export — check an asset's tier BEFORE building around it), and **billing/cancellation\ncomplaints** (manage via app store; mind the trial window).\n\n## The licensing reality (the part most creators skip — this is the moat)\n- **The June 2025 ToS:** content **uploaded/synced** to CapCut's servers grants ByteDance a *nonexclusive,\n  perpetual, royalty-free, worldwide, transferable, sublicensable* license — plus use of your name/image/likeness\n  to identify you, including in sponsored content. You **keep copyright** (it's a license, not ownership — state\n  it precisely, don't fearmonger). The key nuance: it attaches to **uploaded** content; local-only editing\n  without cloud sync/backups likely avoids it. (per the ToS text + async/eesel analyses; verify current terms.)\n- **For client/NDA/agency work:** local editing only, no cloud sync of client assets — or use an editor with\n  licensing safety (Resolve/Premiere). A broad platform license can breach client IP agreements; high-stakes →\n  counsel (not legal advice).\n- **The music trap:** free-library assets are **personal-use only**; paid tiers broaden the license — but even\n  tracks labeled **\"Commercial use\" are reported licensed for TikTok/CapCut platforms only**, and can trigger\n  claims on YouTube/Instagram (per pixflow/Flowith; **verify per track**). Users bear responsibility (and\n  indemnify) for what they upload.\n\n## House metrics\nWatch-through / 3s hold / completion on the published posts (native) — the edit's job is retention; never\nfabricate a metric.\n"
